title: investigate_reveals
---

Narrator: The scouts return with more than you sent them for.


Narrator: You expected standard survey data.
Orbital periods.
Resource density.
Defensive infrastructure.


Narrator: That's all here.

But there's something else at the edges of the report.


Narrator: Not a conclusion.

A shape of something.


Narrator: Energy readings that don't match the declared installations.

Sensor interference that follows a pattern too consistent to be natural.

Historical entries that were altered — not removed, just changed.

Subtly.


Narrator: Whoever maintained this system wanted it to appear a certain way.


Narrator: They were almost successful.


Narrator: Almost.


-> [Review the report carefully]
    Narrator: You go through it again.

    Narrator: Slower this time.

    Narrator: Looking for what they wanted you to miss.


-> [File it and move on]
    Narrator: You mark it for deeper review later.

    Narrator: For now, the intelligence is enough.

===

title: investigate_quiet
---

Narrator: The scouts come back clean.


Narrator: Which means one of two things.


Narrator: Either there is genuinely nothing to find.

Or there is nothing that wanted to be found.


Narrator: You have no way to tell the difference.

That's the problem with good concealment.


Narrator: The absence of information is not the same as the presence of safety.


Narrator: You file the report under inconclusive.

You've accumulated quite a few of those.


-> [Acknowledge]

===

title: investigate_commit
---
Narrator: Reconnaissance order sent.

Eyes on the system. Listen more than you look. The details that matter are never on the surface.

Return with something useful.
===
